# Live counter

**Audience:** application author.
**Prerequisites:** [commands and live tutorial](/docs/tutorials/commands-and-live/).
**Concepts:** [one-shot versus live](/docs/concepts/one-shot-versus-live/).

The shared-view sibling of the [counter](/examples/counter/). Same SQLite card,
but `@live` generates `GET /sse`. Increment and reset are `@command` handlers: Datastar
receives **empty SSE** (200 `text/event-stream`, zero events), and `curl` without
`Datastar-Request` receives `{"count":N}`.
The stream morphs `#counter` and `#counter-feed` in every connected tab.
Reset is optional on the island (`show_reset`); the home page omits it.
Place may come from the browser timezone or a chosen picker value (marked
**chosen** in the feed). Clients can set either freely — this is not verified.

This same app is composed into the [rocci.dev home page](/) via
`@render LiveCounterUi.CounterIsland(...)` (UI module) and
`[http].service` → `LiveCounter.rocci` (SQLite, `@live`, commands). Because
the home page receives a fragment rather than this app's `<body>`, it also
opens `GET /sse` explicitly with
`data-init=@get("/sse", [OpenWhenHidden(True)])`.

This catalog row is `hosting = "live"`. The public demo origin is planned at
[live-counter.examples.rocci.dev](https://live-counter.examples.rocci.dev)
until a staging deploy has served it. It is a separate hostname so it does not
share `/actions/` or `/sse` with the rocci.dev home island.

[Open live demo](https://live-counter.examples.rocci.dev) (planned).

Full file: [LiveCounter.rocci](/examples/live-counter/source/LiveCounter-rocci/).

## Run locally

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/standalone/live-counter/LiveCounter.rocci
```

Open the printed URL in two windows. Click Increment in one; the other updates
the count and the click feed without a refresh.

## Smoke

```sh
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/ | grep -E 'datastar.js|id="counter"|/sse'
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/counter/increment
# {"count":1}
curl -s -D - -o /dev/null -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/counter/increment \
  -H 'Datastar-Request: true'
# HTTP/1.1 200 OK  Content-Type: text/event-stream  (empty body / zero events)
```
